  "solution": {
    "text": "According to bent rule more electronegative atom occupy less s-character so bond length increases. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> bond will be short than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math> bond due to small size of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math>. Correspondingly,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>&nbsp;bond in hydrogen peroxide will be shorter than that of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>. Corresponding structures are:<br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0010_c23413bd4d98.png\" style=\"width: 273px; height: 282px;\" />"
  }
